      "heading": "THE 6 CHECKS",
      "backgroundColor": "#FFFFFF",
      "callsToAction": [],
      "text": "THE 6 CHECKS 01 Whale concentration Share held by the single largest wallet. red ≥ 30% 02 Top holders 2–11 Share held by wallets ranked 2 to 11 combined. red ≥ 40% 03 First-minute buys Buy pressure in the first minute of the tracked window. red ≥ 300 04 Pool liquidity USD liquidity in the pool at verdict time. red < $10k 05 Coin age Minutes since the mint was created on-chain. warn < 15 min 06 Linked wallets · AI Jev estimates how coordinated the holder wallets look. red ≥ 70%",
      "layout": "centered",
      "assetUrls": []
    },
    {
      "selector": "div",
      "type": "content",
      "x": 446,
      "y": 824,
      "width": 1028,
      "height": 217,
      "heading": "THE AI JUDGE",
      "backgroundColor": "#FFFFFF",
      "callsToAction": [],
      "text": "THE AI JUDGE The Jev judge (jev-latest) reads all six checks plus wallet-coordination signals and issues red / yellow / green with probabilities, a coordination score, and a severity rating. One failing check means red unless the judge finds strong counter-evidence. Green needs everything at once: whale under 15%, liquidity over $100k, age over 15 minutes. Outcomes settle automatically: dead means the price fell 90%+ from first sight, liquidity drained under $1,000, or the price sat frozen with zero trading. Unresolved coins count down on the board; resolved coins stay 7 days. Holder data come",
      "layout": "centered",
      "assetUrls": []
    }
